WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.662
Unit 2 is the guide's Step
10, the operating model.

2
00:00:03.662 --> 00:00:08.325
Its DDoS runbook is design guidance,
built on Learn's response strategy.

3
00:00:08.325 --> 00:00:11.389
The under-attack alert
pages the security monitor,

4
00:00:11.389 --> 00:00:14.525
and Defender for Cloud
raises the mitigation alert.

5
00:00:14.525 --> 00:00:16.753
The monitor checks application health,

6
00:00:16.753 --> 00:00:19.520
and the firewall logs for
a layer seven component,

7
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.178
with the top-talker queries from Learn's
page on application layer DDoS protection;

8
00:00:24.178 --> 00:00:28.700
the platform owner lowers the rate limits
through an emergency change if needed.

9
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.513
If mitigation isn't enough,

10
00:00:30.513 --> 00:00:35.375
open a severity A request for Rapid
Response, under Network Protection.

11
00:00:35.375 --> 00:00:38.491
Afterwards: the mitigation
logs, the timeline,

12
00:00:38.491 --> 00:00:42.100
any cost-protection claim,
and an after-action report.

13
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:47.106
The review calendar is design guidance
too: the exposure register weekly;

14
00:00:47.106 --> 00:00:52.358
compliance, exemptions and firewall
false positives monthly; coverage, cost,

15
00:00:52.358 --> 00:00:56.132
firewall rules, vault access
and the rule set quarterly;

16
00:00:56.132 --> 00:01:01.138
failover and a vault restore twice a
year; and a DDoS simulation every year.

17
00:01:01.138 --> 00:01:03.580
The guide's RACI names who does each.
